    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The U.S. Geological Survey in cooperation with the Lake Mead/Mohave Research Institute, University of Nevada, Las Vegas completed a detailed geophysical mapping of the floor of Lake Mead during 1999, 2000, and 2001. The 1999 survey covered the Boulder Basin section of the lake, the 2000 survey focused on the northwestern portion of Las Vegas Bay, and the 2001 survey covered the eastern part of the lake (Fig. 1). Results from these surveys have been presented in several reports (Cross and Twichell, 2003a; 2003b; 2003c; Twichell and others, 1999; 2001); however, here the three data sets have been integrated and are presented as a composite of the entire lake. This Geologic discussion section provides a brief geologic overview of the floor of Lake Mead, as well as summarizing some of the findings resulting from these surveys. This information is provided to provide a geologic perspective for the GIS that accompanies this report.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
